    "source_file": "images/nxl_2026_midwest_2d_labeled.jpg",
    "colour": "Body and detail colour are sampled from the official map inside each bunker's own measured blob, so a neighbour that merely overlaps the bounding box cannot colour the answer. Snake-beam sections carry the blue joint colour detected when the beam was split, which a red-masked section cannot see for itself.",
    "method": "Printed 10-ft grid detected in the image (16 verticals x 13 horizontals = 15 x 12 cells), giving 31.113 px/ft on x and 31.108 px/ft on y. Each bunker is the centre of its own measured paint footprint in that frame. Snake-beam sections are split at the blue joints printed on the beam.",
